        "comments": "This project presents the diploid genome assembly of the hawfinch, Coccothraustes coccothraustes, with a sample provided by Jan T. Lifjeld. The data generation and assembly were carried out by EBP-Nor (https://www.ebpnor.org/). The bCocCoc1.1 assembly is based on 31x PacBio HiFi and 44x Arima Hi-C data. The HiFi reads were filtered for adapters using HiFiAdapterFilt and assembled with hifiasm together with Hi-C data to generate a pair of haplotype-resolved assemblies. K-mers from the two assemblies were used to filter Hi-C reads to create two sets of reads for scaffolding the assemblies, ensuring that reads for hap1 scaffolding did not contain k-mers unique to hap2, and vice versa. YaHS was used for scaffolding. FCS-adaptor was used to remove putative adapters and putative contaminants were removed with FCS-GX. The chromosomes, as confirmed by Hi-C data, are named according to size. Both sex chromosomes have been included in hap1.",
